#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "fc5fc31e-f585-5d15-8a8a-eb0d19704e9a" :question/math-academy-id "e-2947" :question/problem "Find the area of the triangle $\\triangle ABC$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/3b4d9c9c491ffbfc0029c8dc8fbdec5f.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nb &= AB \\\\\n&= AH + HB \\\\\n&= 6 + 3 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n$h={CH} = 4$.\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{b \\cdot h}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9 \\cdot 4}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{36}{2} \\\\\n&= 18\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105465 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "cdb1d145-6e8a-5213-a7f7-8076440cbbeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2949" :question/problem "What is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/6e33b27de00dd277467a671bfd437fe1.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since\n\n$$\nm\\angle{A}=m\\angle{C}\n$$\n\nwe have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC$.\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2}AB \\cdot BC \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 8 \\cdot 8 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 8^{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 64 \\\\\n&= 32\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/id #uuid "58e1ce31-f6fc-5900-ab89-e00241045b12" :question/math-academy-id "e-2950" :question/problem "Consider the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle CDE$ shown below. If the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25 \\textrm{cm}^2$, find the area of $\\triangle ABC$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/da9f32aef805e352321a281de43fe6ef.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $\\triangle CDE$. We can see that $\\overline{CD}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overline{DE}$ and that\n\n$$\nDE=10\\textrm{cm}\n$$\n\nSince the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25\\textrm{cm}^2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{b \\cdot h}{2} \\\\\n25 &= \\frac{10 \\cdot CD}{2} \\\\\n25 &= 5 \\cdot CD \\\\\nCD &= 5cm\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overline{CD}$ is also the height of $\\triangle ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overline{AB}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1397/Source/Images/007cd77422021914a9dee871680fdecb.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $\\triangle ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{b \\cdot h}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{AB \\cdot CD}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{6 \\cdot 5}{2} \\\\\n&= 15cm^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4a3b44b-f034-50b3-b0e3-300e2ba46a56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104412} {:answer/id #uuid "de0ab294-9c50-55c3-a021-e4e6516dde36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10cm^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104413} {:answer/id #uuid "21021f18-c033-581d-bccf-251b62f93963" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12cm^{2}" :db/id 